        "output": "✔ v2 upgrade clears old authentication secrets and management sessions while preserving background tunnels (81.3062ms)\n✔ an interrupted v2 upgrade rolls back its secret removal and session changes atomically (59.2478ms)\n✔ legacy administrators consolidate without deleting accounts, devices or history (54.9629ms)\n✔ the earliest public database upgrades additively through every migration (51.2053ms)\n✔ assist invitation migration preserves endpoints and revokes codes with their host (49.0478ms)\n✔ cross-account migration preserves live legacy sessions and their foreign keys (47.0699ms)\n✔ access mode migration preserves old invitations and revokes fixed access on account rotation (47.4434ms)\n✔ the L4 migration copies legacy TCP and mirrors canonical TCP/UDP fields (47.8096ms)\n✔ RD reconnect migration preserves prior recovery attempts independently of display epochs (48.9583ms)\n✔ a file backup restores data and can continue to accept writes (228.4671ms)\n✔ a failed migration rolls back its schema and migration journal atomically (1.7888ms)\n✔ tunnel diagnostic migration keeps existing runtime rows and leaves the new column empty (45.9257ms)\nℹ tests 12\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 12\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\nℹ duration_ms 946.5211\n",
        "scope": "Exact committed migration SQL executed against real in-memory SQLite fixtures, including MFA-enabled account upgrade, old session revocation, preserved background device and tunnels, and transaction rollback. This supplements successful exact-commit Server CI."
      }
